<p>Because the building sits on one of Barcelona's busiest shopping streets, it's worth allowing extra pavement time around Casa Batlló itself, particularly with young children or a wheelchair user in the group, as the immediate stretch of Passeig de Gràcia can get crowded at midday. Combining the visit with a walk to La Pedrera afterward is easy on foot, and if your itinerary includes several stops in one day, our <a href="/hourly-chauffeur/">hourly chauffeur service</a> lets the same driver wait and move with you between them rather than booking separate one-way trips.</p>
